cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use SAGE, the CNSR metric, or the experimental results in your
  research, please cite the IEEE Transactions on Artificial Intelligence
  article (preferred-citation below).
title: "SAGE: A Stabilize-Assess-Govern-Enforce Framework for Deployment-Oriented Evaluation of LLM-Based Autonomous Agents"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of SAGE, a four-pillar framework for
  deployment-oriented analysis of LLM-based autonomous agents. Stabilize models
  the agent loop as a closed-loop system and relates three sufficient stability
  conditions - observation fidelity, progress monotonicity, and bounded context
  noise - to monitorable failure indicators. Assess combines a behavioral
  autonomy taxonomy with the Cost-Normalized Success Rate (CNSR), a
  ratio-valued metric reporting successful completions per dollar of measured
  operating cost. Govern organizes deployment incidents through a ten-class
  failure taxonomy and a STRIDE analysis of the Model Context Protocol (MCP)
  and Agent-to-Agent (A2A) boundaries. Enforce adds an Adaptive Stability
  Controller that consumes monitor signals and dispatches bounded interventions.
  The repository contains the framework code, the paper's experiments, the
  committed result artifacts, and the scripts that regenerate every table and
  figure.
